    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "Hegarty Properties is delighted to present Rathóg to the market, an exceptional detached family residence of approximately 444.9 sq m (4,789 sq ft), set within beautifully landscaped grounds of c. 0.74 acre at Ballintubber, perfectly positioned between Midleton and Carrigtwohill and minutes from Fota Island Resort.\r\nTaking its name from an old ringfort in the locality, Rathóg was built in 2008 to exacting standards, with no expense spared. Its striking stone and render façade, arched entrance and granite window sills give the house real presence on approach, while inside, a clever split-level design, mezzanine landing and varied ceiling heights create a home that feels both grand and genuinely welcoming.\r\nThe heart of the home is the magnificent kitchen/dining room, with hand-crafted Celtic Interiors solid oak units, granite worktops, a Stanley range and a raised dining area, flowing through to a cosy snug with a newly installed wood-burning stove. A double-height marble hallway with a solid teak staircase with an elegant runner, a generous dual-aspect living room and a triple-aspect studio/office complete a ground floor made for family life and entertaining alike.\r\nUpstairs, four double bedrooms include a superb principal suite with a private balcony overlooking the countryside, a walk-in dressing room and en suite. A second-floor XL playroom offers wonderful flexibility for growing families, teenagers or work-from-home living.\r\nRathóg has been meticulously maintained and thoughtfully upgraded by the current owners – including a new boiler (2025), new bunded oil tank (2024), whole-house water filtration, new high-pressure water pump (2026), new contemporary lighting (2025) and a newly installed wood-burning stove and atomiser fire– so the next owners can simply move in and enjoy.\r\nOutside, electric gates open onto a sweeping, lit driveway and mature, fully landscaped gardens with a westerly rear aspect, a paved patio, built-in BBQ area and a bespoke waterfall – a private, idyllic countryside setting just minutes from the N25."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Accommodation",
        "SortOrder": 1,
        "Content": "GROUND FLOOR\r\nEntrance Porch   \r\nA bright, welcoming porch with tiled flooring. The front door is framed by decorative side glazing with a fanlight overhead, and double doors lead through to the entrance hall.\r\nEntrance Hall   \r\nAn impressive double-height hallway with polished marble tiling, a feature solid teak staircase with elegant cotton bound stairway runner, recessed lighting, large glass ball chandelier and coving to the ceiling, overlooked by the galleried landing above.\r\nLiving Room   \r\nA beautifully proportioned, dual-aspect reception room with solid oak flooring, an elegant bay window and coving to the ceiling. A contemporary child-safe atomiser fire forms the focal point. Double doors with side glazing open to the rear, and glazed double doors lead to the studio/office.\r\nStudio / Home Office   \r\nA bright, triple-aspect room with solid oak flooring and a vaulted ceiling – ideal as a home office, studio, gym or additional family sun room.\r\nKitchen / Dining Room  \r\nThe true heart of the home. A stunning hand-crafted Celtic Interiors solid oak kitchen with granite worktops and a large centre island, double sink with two drainers, freestanding Stanley range, integrated De Dietrich oven and microwave, and fitted for two dishwashers. Marble tiled flooring, feature steps up to a raised dining area, double doors to the rear patio, recessed lighting, Nordlux LED pendant lighting and coving to the ceiling. Reverse osmosis water filter.\r\nSnug   \r\nA cosy retreat off the kitchen with solid walnut flooring, a dramatic double-height ceiling, contemporary, minimalist ring-shaped Arcchio LED chandelier and a wood-burning stove installed in August 2025 – perfect for relaxed family evenings.\r\nUtility Room   \r\nA highly practical utility (the ideal boot room) with an abundance of full-length fitted units, worktop, single drainer sink, space for an additional tall freezer, cosy airing cupboard, plumbing for washing machine and dryer, and a door to the rear garden.\r\nGuest Shower Room  (located off the Utility)\r\nFully tiled, with a three-piece suite, large shower with electric shower unit and heated towel rail.\r\nFIRST FLOOR\r\nLanding   \r\nAn impressive, light-filled mezzanine landing with solid walnut flooring.\r\nGalleried Landing   \r\nOverlooking the entrance hall, with a secondary staircase linking to the split-level bedroom wing and XL playroom/teen hangout space.\r\nPrincipal Bedroom   \r\nA spacious double bedroom to the rear with solid walnut flooring and double doors, framed by side glazing, opening onto a private balcony with glorious views over the surrounding countryside.\r\nWalk-in Dressing Room   \r\nAccessed through an arch from the bedroom, with solid walnut flooring and fully fitted units offering an abundance of hanging and shelving space. Also features attic with a Stira.\r\nEn Suite   \r\nFully tiled, with a three-piece suite including a high-pressure shower, WHB with fitted storage beneath and heated towel rail.\r\nBedroom 2   \r\nA generous double bedroom to the rear with solid walnut flooring and a Velux roof light. Includes “nook” style walk-in attic. \r\n\r\nFamily Bathroom   \r\nA luxurious, fully tiled family bathroom with a large two-person Jacuzzi bath set on raised marble steps, a large high-pressure shower, WHB with fitted storage and marble worktop, and WC.\r\nSPLIT-LEVEL WING\r\nBedroom 3   \r\nA double bedroom overlooking the front with fitted wardrobes and solid oak flooring.\r\nBedroom 4   \r\nA large double bedroom to the front with laminate oak flooring.\r\nEn Suite   \r\nFully tiled, with a three-piece suite and high-pressure shower.\r\nXL Hot Press   \r\nA walk-in hot press with excellent storage and warmth for airing. Water expansion vessel replaced September 2026.\r\nSECOND FLOOR\r\nLanding   \r\nXL Playroom   \r\nA superb, versatile space with two Velux roof lights and a gable window – ideal as a playroom, teen den, cinema room or home office.\r\nStorage   \r\nUseful walk-in storage room, with shelving.\r\n\r\nOutside\r\n\r\nRathóg is approached through electric gates and a recessed entrance, with a sweeping, lit gravel driveway leading to the house and providing ample parking. The grounds of c. 0.74 acre have been fully landscaped to a premium standard, with large lawns, well-maintained flower beds and an abundance of mature shrubs, trees and hedgerow offering wonderful privacy, combined with a host of family spaces.  \r\n\r\nThe westerly rear aspect makes the most of the afternoon and evening sun. A paved patio and outdoor entertainment area features a built-in BBQ with chimney and a bespoke waterfall, set amid stepped hard and soft landscaping. A secure family garden includes a shed and dog kennel, and durable dawn-to-dusk timed Fumagalli exterior lighting lines the driveway. \r\nThe spacious garden also offers ample scope for growing seasonal fruit, vegetables and herbs, overall combining elegant outdoor living with a more self-sufficient lifestyle."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Features",
        "SortOrder": 3,
        "Content": "Build & Finish\r\n•\tBuilt in 2008 to a premium standard, with stone and render façade and granite window sills\r\n•\tSplit-level design with mezzanine and galleried landings\r\n•\tSolid teak staircase and polished marble hall\r\n•\tSolid walnut flooring to the snug, landing, principal suite and Bedroom 2\r\n•\tSolid oak flooring to the living room, studio/office and split-level Bedroom 3, with laminate oak flooring to the Bedroom 4.\r\n•\tFully finished interiors, painted throughout in 2022\r\n•\tNew modern lighting installed December 2025, including Nordlux LED fittings in the kitchen and snug\r\n•\tHillarys blinds and curtains throughout\r\n•\tCentral vacuum system\r\nKitchen\r\n•\tHand-crafted Celtic Interiors solid oak kitchen with granite worktops and large island\r\n•\tStanley range; De Dietrich integrated oven and microwave\r\n•\tFitted for two dishwashers\r\nHeating & Energy\r\n•\tBER B2 (No. 113561559)\r\n•\tOil-fired central heating – new boiler August 2025, new bunded oil tank August 2024\r\n•\tNew thermostats throughout, with timed heating and holiday mode\r\n•\tWood-burning stove in the snug (installed August 2025)\r\n•\tChild-safe atomiser fire in the living room (installed August 2025)\r\nWater\r\n•\tMains water supply\r\n•\tWhole-house carbon water filtration, plus reverse osmosis filter for drinking water\r\n•\tHigh-pressure showers throughout; high-pressure water pump replaced August 2026\r\n•\tHot press water expansion vessel replaced September 2026\r\n•\tSeptic tank emptied and serviced September 2026\r\nSafety & Technology\r\n•\tSmoke alarms throughout with app-based remote alerts\r\n•\tHigh-speed fibre broadband available\r\n•\tElectric entrance gates\r\n•\tComprehensive, fully wired security system with internal laser-beam detection and convenient remote monitoring and control via app.\r\nLuxury Touches\r\n•\tTwo-person Jacuzzi bath in the family bathroom\r\n•\tPrivate balcony off the principal bedroom with countryside views\r\n•\tWalk-in dressing room\r\n•\tXL second-floor playroom and XL walk-in hot press\r\n•\tLandscaped gardens with BBQ area, patio and bespoke waterfall"
      },
